1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,920
This walkthrough shows the actual HandOff prototype.

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:06,610
We begin with a sample project file.

3
00:00:06,610 --> 00:00:08,839
The file stays on this device.

4
00:00:08,839 --> 00:00:15,757
The application computes a real SHA two fifty six fingerprint and displays a local receipt.

5
00:00:15,757 --> 00:00:20,061
Local means there is no blockchain transaction attached.

6
00:00:20,061 --> 00:00:22,875
The receipt can be downloaded as JSON.

7
00:00:22,875 --> 00:00:28,959
Here, it contains the file size and fingerprint, along with convenience metadata.

8
00:00:28,959 --> 00:00:33,978
The Anchor on devnet button offers the optional wallet transaction.

9
00:00:33,978 --> 00:00:40,747
This walkthrough does not execute a wallet transaction or show a simulated chain success.

10
00:00:40,747 --> 00:00:46,829
We import the downloaded receipt and the original report in the verification workspace.

11
00:00:46,829 --> 00:00:51,285
After comparison, the application reports that the file matches.

12
00:00:51,285 --> 00:00:58,853
The result explicitly says that this is a local receipt, so the time of first recording cannot be verified.

13
00:00:58,853 --> 00:01:05,058
Now we import an edited version of the report and compare it against the same receipt.

14
00:01:05,058 --> 00:01:08,636
The application reports that the file has changed.

15
00:01:08,636 --> 00:01:15,060
This is an actual comparison of two different files, not a hardcoded blockchain response.

16
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:17,469
Both files remain in the browser.

17
00:01:17,469 --> 00:01:21,532
The core handover check works without an account or wallet.

18
00:01:21,532 --> 00:01:27,415
The next integration check is a real devnet memo transaction with a connected wallet.

19
00:01:27,415 --> 00:01:32,878
Chain verification checks the successful memo and signing wallet independently.

20
00:01:32,878 --> 00:01:37,290
This prototype does not prove ownership or store project files.
